# Weaver Remote Execution

Weavers are remote execution sessions managed by Loom server and exposed through CLI + web routes.

## 1. Authenticate and list existing weavers

```bash
loom --server-url https://loom.ghuntley.com login
loom --server-url https://loom.ghuntley.com weaver ps
```

## 2. Create a weaver

```bash
loom --server-url https://loom.ghuntley.com weaver new \
  --image ghcr.io/your-org/loom-weaver:latest \
  --repo https://github.com/your-org/your-repo \
  --branch main \
  --ttl 4
```

Alias form is also supported:

```bash
loom --server-url https://loom.ghuntley.com new --image ghcr.io/your-org/loom-weaver:latest
```

## 3. Attach interactively

```bash
loom --server-url https://loom.ghuntley.com weaver attach <weaver-id>
```

Alias form:

```bash
loom --server-url https://loom.ghuntley.com attach <weaver-id>
```

## 4. Use SSH/tunnel transport when required

```bash
loom ssh <weaver-id>
loom tunnel up --weaver <weaver-id>
loom tunnel status
loom tunnel down
```

Device lifecycle (WireGuard):

```bash
loom wg devices list
loom wg devices register --name "build-laptop"
loom wg devices revoke <device-id>
```

## 5. Clean up stale environments

```bash
loom --server-url https://loom.ghuntley.com weaver delete <weaver-id>
```

<Callout variant="tip" title="Operational visibility">
	Use `/weavers` and `/weavers/:weaverId` in web UI for state inspection alongside CLI control.
</Callout>

## Failure triage checklist

- `401 Unauthorized`: run `loom login` against the same `--server-url`.
- Immediate exit after create: verify image entrypoint runs a long-lived process.
- Attach failure: verify the weaver still appears in `loom weaver ps`.
